B.c3c=new A.qg("A Revelation, Not a Book First","The Qur'an arrived as sound before it was paper: Jibril brought it to the Prophet \ufdfa over twenty-three years, and the first word of the first revelation was Iqra \u2014 read (96:1). It lived in recitation and memory long before it lived on shelves.","Qur'an 96:1","/quran","Open the reader")
B.c34=new A.qg("Guarded, Word by Word","'Indeed, it is We who sent down the Qur'an, and indeed We will be its guardian' (15:9). The protection Allah promised was not of a copy but of the text itself \u2014 memorized by millions, letter by letter, in every generation.","Qur'an 15:9",null,null)
B.c3a=new A.qg("Why Arabic","'We have sent it down as an Arabic Qur'an that you might understand' (12:2). The language is not a barrier around the meaning \u2014 it is the vessel of it. Even a little Arabic learned with love changes how the verses land.","Qur'an 12:2",null,null)
B.aHk=s([B.c3c,B.c34,B.c3a],t.pt)
B.c3d=new A.R3("How the Qur'an Came",B.aHk)
B.c38=new A.qg("Translation Is a Bridge, Not the Land","Every translation is an interpretation wearing the translator's glasses. Read yours with gratitude and with a light grip \u2014 when a word carries your whole heart, check what the Arabic actually says. The app shows both for exactly this reason.","Reading practice",null,null)
B.c3b=new A.qg("Recite With Measured Beauty","'And recite the Qur'an with measured recitation' (73:4). Slow enough to hear yourself. Understanding grows in the pause between verses, not in the race through them.","Qur'an 73:4","/quran","Practice in the reader")
B.c36=new A.qg("None Touch It Except the Purified","'Indeed, it is a noble Qur'an, in a Register well-protected; none touch it except the purified' (56:77-79). Begin with wudu, begin with ta'awwudh, begin with His name \u2014 the body taught the reverence the heart then keeps.","Qur'an 56:77-79",null,null)
B.aCy=s([B.c38,B.c3b,B.c36],t.pt)
B.c3f=new A.R3("Reading With Meaning",B.aCy)
B.c37=new A.qg("A Fixed Portion, However Small","The most beloved deeds to Allah are the most consistent, even if small (Bukhari 6464). A standard mushaf has 604 pages, so one page a day finishes the Qur'an in about twenty months. Small and daily beats large and abandoned \u2014 always.","Sahih al-Bukhari 6464",null,null)
B.c39=new A.qg("Healing and Mercy","'And We send down of the Qur'an that which is healing and mercy for the believers' (17:82). Some verses are medicine for specific griefs \u2014 the Prophet \ufdfa recited over the sick. Find the verse that answers your season and keep it near.","Qur'an 17:82",null,null)
B.c35=new A.qg("The Complaint of the Qur'an","The Prophet \ufdfa said the Qur'an will complain on the Last Day: 'O my Lord, indeed my people have taken this Qur'an as [a thing] abandoned' (25:30). Abandonment is not only never opening it \u2014 it is opening it and hearing nothing. Read one verse today as if it were addressed to you. It is.","Qur'an 25:30",null,null)
B.aIK=s([B.c37,B.c39,B.c35],t.pt)
B.c3e=new A.R3("The Qur'an in a Day",B.aIK)
B.ayr=s([B.c3d,B.c3f,B.c3e],A.ac("y<R3>"))
